\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 City Attorney Michael Gates presented a PowerPoint Presentation titled: Proposal for Expanded Prosecution of Illegal Businesses and Business-Related Nuisance with slides entitled: Proposal for Expanded Prosecution of Illegal Businesses and Business-Related Nuisance, New Law Enforcement Approach, Proposal for Expanded Prosecution of Illegal Businesses and Business-Related Nuisance (3), The Law, Areas of Illegal or Potentially Illegal Businesses, Massage Establishments, Short-Term Rental Homes, Marijuana Dispensaries (2), Unlicensed Sober Living & Treatment Homes (4), Proposal for Expanded Prosecution of Illegal Businesses and Business-Related Nuisance, Areas of Illegal or Potentially Illegal Businesses, and Proposal for Expanded Prosecution of Illegal Businesses and Business-Related Nuisance. \par
\par
CM Delgleize: stated her concern costs of new position and timing regarding budget and staff support from Code Enforcement.  Attorney Gates responded the new hire would help Code Enforcement and this item is in response to the earlier "H" item. Discussion ensued regarding Short Term Rentals.\par
\par
CM Hardy: questioned likelihood of recovering costs, Attorney Gates explained procedure taken. Discussion ensued regarding status (at will) of new position and re-evaluate at a later date.  Ms. Hardy stated her support this item be considered at a later time as part of the budget process.\par
\par
CM Peterson: questioned if there is money in Attorney's current budget from salary savings due to retirements and job movement in department.  He stated he favors an At-Will employee in the position.\par
\par
CM Semeta: Described the types of activities which would be targeted and agreed the position should be At-Will.\par
\par
CM O'Connell: His position is to wait and see\par
\par
CM Brenden: expected to see more Code Enforcement help and stated the need for the extra help in that department. questioned program working with county District Attorney's office/Attorney Gates described how division of labor works.  More discussion regarding priorities on prosecuting illegal business based on complaints and city's policy.\par
\par
Posey substitute - MOU with county/update on position/ part of budget process - get more details\par
